      "The Unavoidable Truth: A network that doesn't provide care is not insurance; it is a financial extraction mechanism.\n\nThe Unavoidable Lie: That the insurance company is providing a service when they are merely providing a list.",
      "Alethekanon:\nThe business model relies on the friction of access. By creating a 'ghost network,' the insurer minimizes payouts while maximizing premiums. This is a deliberate structural failure.",
      "Awwthekanon:\nIt is devastating that someone reaching out for help is met with a cold, automated system that leads nowhere. Everyone deserves to be heard and supported when they are at their lowest.",
