      "Advisory groups are often the bridge between policy and reality, yet they frequently struggle to translate lived experience into actionable systemic change.\nEvidence: inclusive policy, bureaucratic friction, stalled progress\n#Autism #NDIS",
      "The stated purpose of the Autism Advisory Group is to provide expert, lived-experience guidance to the NDIS to ensure policies are effective and equitable for the autistic community.\nStated Judgement: (+0.5, +0.5) — Greater Good",
      "In reality, the group often functions as a consultative layer that lacks the power to override administrative directives, resulting in a neutral, static impact on actual policy outcomes.\nResulting Judgement: (0.0, 0.0) — Neutral",
