      "The Autism Advisory Group serves as a formal mechanism for the NDIS to engage with the autistic community. It is designed to ensure that the voices of those directly affected by policy are heard at the highest levels of decision-making.",
      "The Bright Side:\nHaving a dedicated advisory group is a significant step forward from total exclusion, providing a formal channel for feedback that didn't exist previously.",
      "The Breakdown & Plane Error:\nThe error is in the WHO (the operator). The group is an advisory body, not an executive one. It lacks the authority to enforce its recommendations, leading to a disconnect between advice and implementation.",
      "The Trajectory: The Path of Redemption.\nWhen you map the gap between the stated intent of influence and the actual effect of consultation...",
      "...it plots a trajectory toward Lesser Good, provided the group can move from passive advice to active, measurable policy influence.",
