      "...it plots a trajectory toward a more balanced, if currently stalled, educational model.",
      "The Unavoidable Truth: Play is not a break from learning; it is the primary mechanism for human cognitive and social development.\n\nThe Unavoidable Lie: That academic rigor is inversely proportional to time spent in unstructured play.",
      "Alethekanon:\nThe system is optimizing for the wrong metric. By prioritizing short-term data over long-term cognitive architecture, it creates a deficit that will manifest in future social and creative capacity.",
      "Awwthekanon:\nIt breaks my heart to think of children losing their chance to just be kids. Their laughter and curiosity are the seeds of their future, and we must protect that space for them to grow.",
      "Brothekanon:\nLook, you can't just cram a kid's brain like a hard drive. They need to run around and break stuff—metaphorically—to figure out how the world works. Let them play, or you're just building robots, not people."
