      "The persistent cultural obsession with Marilyn Monroe reveals more about our current lack of icons than it does about the star herself. \n\nIn @nytopinion.nytimes.com\nEvidence: cultural nostalgia, artistic legacy, modern void",
      "The claim is that Monroe remains a uniquely fulgent and seductive figure in a world lacking such powerful artistic presence. \nStated Judgement: (+0.5, 0.0) — Good Preference",
