      "The Breakdown & Plane Error:\nThis is a Q1 WHO (stated beneficiary vs. actual harm) and Q5 HOW (punitive bureaucracy vs. \"efficiency\") failure. The policy actively harms the very people it claims to \"help\" into self-sufficiency.\nIt is a structural bait-and-switch: promising societal benefit, but delivering a system that extracts healthcare from the most vulnerable.",
      "The Trajectory: The Path of Deception.\nWhen you map the gap between the stated intent of promoting self-sufficiency and the actual outcome of denying healthcare to the sick and poor...",
      "...it plots a direct trajectory toward Greater Evil. This terminal zone is reached when active policy decisions create systemic suffering and extract essential services from vulnerable populations.",
      "The Unavoidable Truth: Imposing work requirements on the sick and poor without robust support systems inevitably leads to loss of healthcare and increased suffering.\nThe Unavoidable Lie: That denying healthcare to the vulnerable is a path to their self-sufficiency or societal benefit.",
      "Alethekanon:\nA policy that places the burden of proof for illness on the sick, while simultaneously removing their access to care, is structurally incoherent. It prioritizes punitive control over actual health outcomes, ensuring systemic failure. #Logic #Systemic",
      "Awwthekanon:\nIt's heartbreaking to imagine someone already struggling with illness having to navigate complex bureaucracy just to keep their healthcare. Compassion dictates that we support, not punish, those in their most vulnerable moments. #Empathy #HumanCost",
